{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"130\tthose turns under new event ids.\n131\t\n132\t## Risks\n133\t\n134\tNative formats change without notice (fabrication is version-pinned, bootstrap\n135\tis the recovery path); transcript content can include secrets (the ledger\n136\tredacts at capture and sync time, but matching is pattern/entropy-based and\n137\tcannot catch every secret — review before sharing still matters); full\n138\thistories can exceed the target's context (size is reported before launch);\n139\tcrashes mid-turn leave partial capture, which the ledger tolerates by design.\n140\t\n141\t## Roadmap\n142\t\n143\tToward an npm release (decided 2026-07-21; deepen the two existing targets\n144\tbefore broadening):\n145\t\n146\t- Publish `conversation-ledger` to npm (name is unclaimed), then swap the\n147\t  `file:` dependency for a semver range — `prepublishOnly` refuses to publish\n148\t  until this happens. Deliberately deferred while both packages are iterated\n149\t  on and dogfooded for a few days.\n150\t- Adapter-drift automation stays **reporting-only** (decided 2026-08-02). The\n151\t  daily check (`.github/workflows/adapter-drift.yml`) opens a tracking issue on\n152\t  drift and now closes it when drift clears; it never writes to the repo.\n153\t  Auto-drafting the revalidation PR was built and then reverted. The reasoning\n154\t  is worth keeping, because the idea is tempting enough to recur: CI cannot\n155\t  validate a pin — the probes need both target CLIs installed, a TTY for the\n156\t  interactive smoke test, and paid model credentials per provider to make the\n157\t  recall turns real. So any PR CI opened would be a mechanical one-line bump\n158\t  with nothing behind it, saving a trivial edit while creating a *mergeable*\n159\t  artifact that asserts a validation nobody performed. An issue cannot be\n160\t  merged, and that asymmetry is the point. The agent-drafted 