d after running both\n  probes to completion.\n\n## Then update the docs\n\n- `docs/specs/opencode-session-format.md` §8: mark the two closed unknowns\n  RESOLVED in place, each with the date and the opencode version tested,\n  matching the style the claude/codex specs use for their resolved unknowns.\n  Record the measured numbers, not just \"works\".\n- `docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md`, the Roadmap section: the opencode bullet\n  currently ends with \"Remaining opencode gaps: no headless model-recall probe\n  ..., and long histories unmeasured\". Update it to reflect reality.\n- Add the new probe to the roadmap's list of revalidation tooling.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Node 20+, ESM, no new dependencies.\n- Match the surrounding code's style: these probes lead with a comment\n  explaining what question the probe answers and why that question is the\n  right one. Follow that.\n- Do not modify `src/targets/opencode.ts` unless a probe proves an actual\n  adapter bug — if it does, fix it and say so explicitly in the PR.\n- Do not touch the version pins in `scripts/check-adapter-drift.mjs`.\n","replaceAll":false,"structuredPatch":[{"lines":[" "," ## Acceptance criteria"," ","-- `npm test` passes (currently 61 tests, all must still pass).","+- `npm test` passes (currently 88 tests, all must still pass)."," - `npm run build` is clean."," - Both probes actually **executed** against the real opencode binary, with","   their real output pasted into the PR description. Do not open a PR"],"newLines":7,"newStart":69,"oldLines":7,"oldStart":69}],"userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"ddef13b0-84dc-4f9c-a131-3c4af194e326","version":"2.1.221"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-04T03:57:38.435Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
