nuinely low urgency**\n6. **Encrypted-reasoning loose ends:** blob TTL unknown, and whether API-platform-org auth behaves like ChatGPT auth is unverified. A rejected blob at `codex resume` time has no proactive detection — it falls back to `--bootstrap` like any other drift failure.\n7. **Multi-hop reasoning carry-over** — reconstructing an ancestor hop's reasoning via the lineage chain when re-bridging. Explicitly deferred as a follow-up.\n8. **Minor opencode unknowns:** whether the `Model … is not valid` toast affects `--fork` or tool permissioning, and the `project` table's id derivation (if a future release resolves the project from `info.directory`, the lookup could be dropped).\n\nThree things read like todos but are actually **closed decisions**, so I left them off: drift-agent stage 2 (built, reverted, decided reporting-only on 2026-08-02 — CI can't validate a pin without both CLIs, a TTY, and paid credentials); the spec verification gaps (all closed 2026-07-27); and the deliberately-unmeasured set (>300 turns, `custom_tool_call` fabrication, the Claude picker's sort key).\n\nIf you want this to stop living in three places, I can write it into a `TODO.md` — say the word.\n\nresult: Reconstructed turnbridge's todo list from the roadmap, memory, and spec unknowns — 8 open items, with the npm publish chain (cledger to npm → swap the `file:` dep → publish turnbridge) as the only hard release blocker; drift check clean on all three CLI pins.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"173cfc66bb28f4c20e474f522f197eeef0c627de","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:4fc5e727-a1d5-4399-a448-9d24a0ce9c15","seq":58},"id":"ev1-d0f088f925589b6a9cdb1ed14504e80aa28798033cfee6f7cd1cfc3cf7e07cb3","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-04T03:44:48.012Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"4fc5e727-a1d5-4399-a448-9d24a0ce9